Z||000009||Mark||08-10-2001||08:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Gold87SE:<BR><B>It was at night and I went right home. The noise did sound like the fuel pump but really loud. When I started the car the next day, it still made the noise. I drove about a 1/4 mile and ran out of gas. The gauge told me that I had 1/8 of a tank left. When I filled it up, the noise went away so that answered my question.<P>Is it common for the fuel pump to whine really loud when you're just about out of gas?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes.  My fuel pump also made strange noises when I ran really low on fuel the other day.  Easy to mistake the sound too.  I thought it was the rear brakes "groaning" when I stopped hard.  Actually, the gas sloshed forward in the tank, which caused the pump to run dry.<BR>||||reg||1
